{"duration_api_ms":72009,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.5486175999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31873,"cache_read_input_tokens":724348,"output_tokens":7433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":63844,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":283},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":7433,"cacheReadInputTokens":724348,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31873,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5486175999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1328,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":31873,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I ran the before/after timing on deck-50.pptx. The style-cache key path got much faster, but the deck as a whole did not open faster in these runs. Acceptance passed (6/6 suites); `theseus validate` shows 0 errors and 1 warning. Everything is committed as 490294a.\n\n**How I measured:** I used the native Document Server and the CDP profiler. I applied the same `getKey` change to the installed `sdkjs/slide/sdk-all.js`, measured, then put the original file back (`cmp` confirms it is byte-identical). The standard `drawings-functions.js` only counts the drawings code, so it can't see `StyleCache.getKey`, which lives in `word/`. I also ran a scratch copy that counts it, 5 runs each way.\n\n| deck-50.pptx, median ms (inclusive) | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `StyleCache.getKey`, including building the new string key | 111.2 | **23.5** |\n| `CMemory.sha256` | 92.9 | gone |\n| `StyleCache.add` / `remove` | 76.3 / 27.6 | 23.2 / ~0 |\n| `CShape.recalculateTextStyles` | 124.8 | 175.5 |\n| Total busy time during open (median of 5) | 2063 | 2327 |\n\n- **Cost of the new string keys:** building them takes about 23.5 ms, against 111 ms with sha256, so about 88 ms saved in that path.\n- **Not resolved:** `recalculateTextStyles` and total open time did not go down. Runs on this 2-CPU VM vary a lot (busy time 1724–2965 ms), so it may be noise. It may also be that long string keys move cost somewhere else, such as hashing or garbage collection. I recorded this in the log; I did not cover it up.\n\n**Commit fe036d5 for review:** the outer repo doesn't track `external/sdkjs`, and the packet doesn't allow new files. So I pasted the full `git format-patch` of fe036d5 into the packet's Executor log; it applies with `git -C external/sdkjs am`. It is also still on branch `pkt/PKT-0078` of the nested clone. I did not push it to the shared mirror.\n\n**Decisions:** the key is the exact serialized bytes, so it can't collide. As in the earlier attempts, I did not add a per-hierarchy cache in Shape.js: its output also depends on autofit and the fill reference, so I couldn't invalidate it safely within this packet. I added no follow-up packets. The friction line is appended.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- The drawings-by-function profile hides style-cache costs because that code is in `word/`. A key or hashing change needs the wider count.\n- To compare before and after, patch the installed bundle in place with an exact-match replacement and restore it, the way `sdkjs-shape-cache.py` does. A sanctioned script for this is still missing.\n- On this VM, total open time is too noisy to show a gain of about 90 ms. Per-function inclusive times are the reliable signal.","ttft_ms":1664,"type":"result","duration_ms":408801,"uuid":"78ac692c-1d2a-41a0-a0c1-d7e61fc3d62a","ttft_stream_ms":1045,"time_to_request_ms":353,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":231,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":18,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":20,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":42,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":151,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":238,"process_anon_mib_result":146,"process_peak_rss_mib":254,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4939,"process_wall_ms_turn":408801,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1040,"process_wall_ms_streaming":56231,"main_stream_count":13,"main_stream_event_count":1043,"main_stream_chunk_count":676,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":6,"cpu_ms":19,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":6,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1045,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":2000208,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793660695698.1104,"queued_turn_co